  {
   "vocabId": "rom-species-2024:이상해풀",
   "korean": "이상해풀의 등에는 큰 꽃봉오리가 자라요.",
   "gloss": "A large flower bud grows on Ivysaur's back.",
   "targetForm": "이상해풀",
   "areaId": "pallet_town",
   "source": "themed-v1",
   "generator": "llm-claude-opus-4-7",
   "auditFix": {
    "verdict": "mistranslation",
    "issue": "Korean/gloss mismatch introduced by the prior auditFix. The Korean was correctly changed from 새싹 (sprout/seedling) to 꽃봉오리 (flower bud) to match Ivysaur lore, but the English gloss was not updated and still says 'A sprout grows on Ivysaur's back.' 꽃봉오리 means 'flower bud,' not 'sprout' (which would be 새싹). The gloss should be e.g. 'A large flower bud grows on Ivysaur's back.'",
    "evidenceUrl": "https://pokemon.fandom.com/ko/wiki/%EC%9D%B4%EC%83%81%ED%95%B4%ED%92%80_(%ED%8F%AC%EC%BC%93%EB%AA%AC)",
    "auditedAt": "2026-05-09",
    "round": 2,
    "priorAuditFix": {
     "verdict": "polish:fix",
     "issue": "Confirmed Pokemon-lore mismatch: Ivysaur's defining feature is the flower BUD (꽃봉오리) on its back, not a 새싹 (sprout/seedling). The bud is a Rafflesia-like flower bud that releases an aroma when ready to bloom. 새싹 is more apt for Bulbasaur (이상해씨); by Ivysaur stage the plant has progressed to a large bud.",
     "evidenceUrl": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Ivysaur_(Pok%C3%A9mon)",
     "auditedAt": "2026-05-09"
    }
   },
